1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
This is the implementation demo for journey four.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:08,470
It is the real application and API running on this machine, with a synthetic buyer.

3
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:12,650
It shows how a buyer keeps a list of the cars they are comparing.

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,200
A new buyer opens Vehicles and sees an empty list.

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,110
Adding a car opens a dialog.

6
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:24,560
With a short VIN and a short phone number, the dialog lists exactly what to fix,

7
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,290
and each field explains its own problem.

8
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:32,810
A valid car is saved and appears in the list with its odometer, price and seller.

9
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:37,710
Saving the same VIN again is refused, because it is already on the list.

10
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:42,210
Editing a car works the same way, and the changes show right away.

11
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:46,290
Removing a car asks first, and cancel is the focused choice.

12
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,680
Every vehicle belongs to one buyer.

13
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,010
Another buyer who asks for the list does not see it.

14
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:57,040
Asking for that car by its identifier is answered as not found,

15
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,960
and so is trying to delete it.

16
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,590
The owner can read it, and can remove it.

17
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:06,260
The buyer is always taken from the sign in token, never from the request,

18
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:09,910
so there is no way to ask for someone else's car by name.

19
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:13,360
That is true for reading, changing and deleting alike.

20
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:18,300
Removing a car hides it from the list, but nothing is deleted.

21
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:22,880
Inspections you have already booked keep the details they were booked with,

22
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,600
so the history stays intact.

23
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,980
A removed VIN can be saved again later.

24
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:29,850
These rules are covered by the automated tests.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,810
Here is what to remember.

26
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:35,400
Each buyer sees only their own cars.

27
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,860
A VIN can be saved once at a time.

28
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:41,330
Removing hides a car without erasing the record,

29
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:44,500
and past inspections keep their own details.

30
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,540
Next, journey five: pay for an inspection.
